# Dáin, Lord of the Iron Hills with an enduring story: "creatures can't attack you unless their controller pays {1} for
# each of those creatures" (CR 508.1d, 508.1h-j). Bot2 casts Dáin from Mox Pearl and Mox Jet on turn 2, so it controls
# three artifacts and/or legendaries (Dáin, two Moxen) and has an enduring story from then on (storied, CR 702.195a). On
# turn 3 Bot1 declares both Llanowar Elves as attackers: the total cost to attack is {2}, which Bot1 pays by tapping Mox
# Ruby and Mox Sapphire as it is asked for (CR 508.1i-j). Both Elves attack and connect: Bot2 goes to 18, and both Moxen
# are tapped for it. Without the cost the Moxen would stay untapped; without the enduring story likewise.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mox Sapphire
Llanowar Elves
Llanowar Elves
Forest
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Dáin, Lord of the Iron Hills
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Dáin, Lord of the Iron Hills.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot2.EnduringStory = true
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Llanowar Elves; Llanowar Elves)
? Combat.AttackCost = {2}
? Combat.AttackCost.Attackers = Llanowar Elves; Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
[T3 Bot1.Blockers]
? Combat.Attackers = Llanowar Elves > Bot2; Llanowar Elves > Bot2
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

